# Framework provider secrets for /vibe-plan external AI consultation.
# This is NOT your app's .env — vibecode is often layered inside another project,
# and the framework's provider key must never be mixed into that project's .env
# (nor committed with it).
#
# Pick ONE of these (the script checks them in this order):
#   1. Export in your shell rc — machine-global, no file needed:
#        export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
#   2. Machine-global file (RECOMMENDED — set once, works across all projects):
#        mkdir -p ~/.config/vibecode
#        cp .vibecode/providers.env.example ~/.config/vibecode/providers.env
#        # then edit that copy and fill in the key
#   3. Project-local override — copy to `.vibecode/providers.env` (gitignored).
#        ONLY use this if you are sure that path is gitignored in THIS project.
#   4. Any path via $VIBECODE_ENV_FILE=/abs/path/to/providers.env
#
# The key name must match `api_key_env` in .vibecode/config/ai-providers.json.

# DeepSeek — https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
